# Contributing

This application owns its generated source. Use Go 1.27.3, Make and GOWORK=off.
Do not add sibling replacements or depend on the CLI checkout at build time.

`nostosx add api` can extend an existing generated v1 service. Review its Proto
import/RPC edit, messages, external HTTP binding and adapter/test files. Define
payload types, implement the unimplemented RPC and replace the stub test before
exposing it. Regenerate with `make generate`, run `go mod tidy` and check drift.
HTTP mounting, per-operation authorization and CQRS use cases are explicit changes.

```sh
go mod download
make check
make lint
make vulncheck
make api-check
make smoke
```

Install golangci-lint v2.15.0 and govulncheck v1.9.0 outside this module. All
tests and process checks are Go tests. Contract builds use the pinned Go CLI;
once Proto sources exist, install Buf 1.72.0 on PATH.
Generation downloads pinned Go plugins; no system protoc is required.
See README.md for exact generator versions and commands. After changing contracts,
run make generate, go mod tidy and make api-check. Breaking checks need an explicit
versioned Git baseline. Never hand-edit generated Go or OpenAPI output.

Keep domain and application transport-free. Define consumer-owned ports beside
real use cases and compose their implementations in services/<name>/module.go.
Use servex/cqrs when introducing typed commands and queries; middleware belongs
in assembly. Keep service-private adapters under services/<name>/internal.
Do not add speculative infrastructure, fake status use cases or architecture-test
packages to make empty directories look complete.

Test application behavior, cancellation and authorization beside the code.
Use integration-tagged tests for listeners, model fixtures and external adapters.
Every process must release resources on cancellation and failed startup. Keep
fixtures isolated; never use operator model credentials or shared data stores.
API authentication, per-operation authorization, persistence and migrations are
application decisions and must be reviewed with their own regression tests.

GO, GOFMT, NOSTOSX, GOLANGCI_LINT and GOVULNCHECK select executables. Use an
absolute NOSTOSX binary path for source builds; NOSTOSX_VERSION selects a release
for the default go run invocation. No generator source is copied into this project.
Template
upgrades do not automatically update this application; review source changes.
